# Keys whose value in a NON-PROD dotenvx profile (apps/api/.env, .env.dev, .env.staging)
# is allowed to EQUAL the apps/api/.env.prod value — temporarily.
# `pnpm test:envs` fails on any other secret-classed key that matches prod.
# Format: KEY<whitespace>reason. Every entry here is a debt: remove the line once
# the vendor has a per-environment credential and the prod value is rotated.
#
# --- pending per-environment vendor credentials (needs a vendor console) ---
DAYTONA_API_KEY            prod Daytona org; needs a dev org/key, then rotate prod
PIPEDREAM_CLIENT_ID        prod Pipedream project; needs a dev project, then rotate prod
PIPEDREAM_CLIENT_SECRET    prod Pipedream project; needs a dev project, then rotate prod
AWS_SES_ACCESS_KEY_ID      needs a non-prod IAM user (or Mailpit only), then rotate prod
AWS_SES_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY  needs a non-prod IAM user (or Mailpit only), then rotate prod
RESEND_API_KEY             needs a non-prod Resend key, then rotate prod
LIVEKIT_API_KEY            needs a dev LiveKit project, then rotate prod
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET         needs a dev LiveKit project, then rotate prod
TAVILY_API_KEY             spend only; needs a capped dev key, then rotate prod
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY          spend only; needs a capped dev key, then rotate prod
APIFY_TOKEN                spend only; needs a capped dev key, then rotate prod
OPENROUTER_API_KEY         spend only; needs a capped dev key, then rotate prod
SERPER_API_KEY             spend only; needs a capped dev key, then rotate prod
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN        spend only; needs a capped dev key, then rotate prod
ASTER_API_KEY              spend only; needs a capped dev key, then rotate prod
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY      dev/staging carry the PROD IAM user; needs a non-prod IAM user, then rotate prod (HIGH)
MANAGED_GIT_GITHUB_TOKEN   PAT for the managed-git GitHub org; needs a per-env PAT/GitHub App, then rotate prod
# --- must rotate together with the deployed env's AWS Secrets Manager entry ---
REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SECRET  webhook auth header; set a distinct value per env in the RevenueCat dashboard + AWS SM, then rotate prod
INTERNAL_SERVICE_KEY       dev/staging value must match what the deployed dev/staging API injects into sandboxes (AWS SM); local already unique
